summary: configure a thinpool kdump target
description: |
    This case is to configure thin lvm partition as kdump target.
    Alert: It will format the partition mounted at $THIN_MP to thin lvm

    Accept Parameters:
    - THIN_MP: The moint point partition mount at and will be formated to thin LVM
              It will be configured as Kdump dump target
              THIN_MP cannot be '/' or '/boot'
    - THIN_KPATH: The relative path where the vmcore will be dump to.
              By default: '/var/crash'
    - THIN_SIZE: The size of thinpool volumn
              By default: 2G
    - RESTART_KDUMP: Whether kdump service will be restarted after configuring thin
              LVM target. Allowed values: true / false
              Be default: true

contact: Kdump QE <kdump-qe-list@redhat.com>
test: chmod a+x ./runtest.sh; ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
recommend:
  - kexec-tools
require:
  - lvm2
duration: 30m
extra-summary: /kernel/kdump/config-thin
extra-task: /kernel/kdump/config-thin
